      "body": "Hey, I'm Juampi from the Firecrawl team.\n\n`extract-design-md` reads frontend source, which works well when the repo is on disk. When the user only has a URL (a client's current site, a reference site, a product whose code isn't available), there is nothing for the skill to read. In #43 the suggestion was to fold \"extract from a live URL\" into `extract-design-md` as another input mode instead of adding a separate skill. This issue proposes one way to do that.\n\n### Proposal\n\nAdd an optional \"From a live URL\" path to Phase 1, next to the source-code path. A Firecrawl /scrape request with `formats: [\"branding\", \"screenshot\"]` returns the rendered page's palette, fonts, type scale, spacing base unit, button styles and logo as JSON, plus a screenshot URL. Phases 2 and 3 stay as they are: the agent maps those fields onto the same DESIGN.md sections and YAML frontmatter, and reads the screenshot to write the atmosphere paragraph. The source-code path stays the default and nothing changes for people without a Firecrawl API key.\n\n### Real output\n\nRequest (run on 30 Oct 2026):\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/scrape \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $FIRECRAWL_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"url\":\"https://stripe.com\",\"formats\":[\"branding\",\"screenshot\"],\"origin\":\"stitch-skills\"}'\n```\n\nIt returned in 5.2 s with these fields (trimmed):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"colorScheme\": \"light\",\n  \"colors\": {\"primary\": \"#533AFD\", \"secondary\": \"#E5EDF5\", \"background\": \"#FFFFFF\", \"textPrimary\": \"#000000\", \"link\": \"#533AFD\"},\n  \"fonts\": [{\"family\": \"Sohne-Var\", \"role\": \"body\"}, {\"family\": \"SF Pro Display\", \"role\": \"heading\"}],\n  \"typography\": {\"fontSizes\": {\"h1\": \"48px\", \"h2\": \"32px\", \"body\": \"14px\"}},\n  \"spacing\": {\"baseUnit\": 8, \"borderRadius\": \"0px\"},\n  \"components\": {\"buttonPrimary\": {\"background\": \"#533AFD\", \"textColor\": \"#FFFFFF\", \"borderRadius\": \"4px\"}},\n  \"brandName\": \"Stripe\"\n}\n```\n\nThe response also carries the logo, favicon and OG image, and `data.screenshot` is a 1920x1080 PNG. linear.app gave the same shape: dark scheme, `#5E6AD2` primary, `#08090A` background, Inter, h1 64px, base unit 4, 8px radius.\n\nFor comparison, a plain fetch of stripe.com returns 669 KB of HTML with 5 external stylesheets and no `<style>` blocks. The brand hex appears once and the font name once, and there is no type scale or spacing value to read. The branding format returns values read from the rendered page instead.\n\n### Next step\n\nIf the direction works for you, I can put together the change for review. It would touch only `extract-design-md/SKILL.md`: a short \"From a live URL\" section plus a table mapping the branding fields to the frontmatter keys. The Firecrawl API docs for the format are [here](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/features/scrape?utm_source=stitch-skills&utm_medium=integration#extract-brand-identity).",
